    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24189" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intercessus</span></b> , ūs, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an intervention;</i> only in <i>abl. sing.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem intercessu suo servare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 5, 4, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicujus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Salv. Gub. D. 1, p. 27</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intercessu auctoritatis suae prohibere ne,
					etc., Imp. Diocl. et Const. inter Fragm. Jur. Antei. p. 75
					Mai.: temporis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Oros. 5, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
